@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=20&cursor=...` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": ...}`: a page of items ordered by `id`. `limit` is optional and must be an integer from 1 to 100; `cursor` is optional and must be a cursor returned by an earlier response. `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page. Invalid limits or cursors return HTTP 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
